# kit:not-a-real-app
#
# A FIXTURE for the writer's conformance oracle (kit#119), not an app. Each
# behaviour exists to put one of writer.js's splice rules under test: where a
# step lands when comments trail a block, where a review line goes when there is
# none, and which line it replaces when there is.

behaviour BEH-A "Has an actor, a source and an explicit review"
  actor owner
  source inferred notes.md#a
  review unreviewed
  when opens page:Home
  then sees button:Save
# a comment trailing BEH-A, which a new step must land ABOVE

behaviour BEH-B "Has a source and no review line"
  source defined
  when presses button:Save
  then sees region:Saved

behaviour BEH-C "Has only an actor"
  actor owner
  when opens page:Settings

# this comment introduces BEH-D, so nothing may be appended under it

behaviour BEH-D "Has no preamble at all"
  when opens page:About


